[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} {:answer/id #uuid "ab51dc5a-a926-51cd-8e7b-df0870f057c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248946} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cbad19-d246-5b98-8980-41bddf12f22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249448} {:answer/id #uuid "e99bc9d8-a545-56d1-baef-23123e5ae336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{6}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249486} {:answer/id #uuid "f8073886-20e6-5ba4-879b-63835b53eb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9a9941-4c05-5900-9e9e-c028b2cee8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64685827-c31f-5450-80d9-3d65e9e828de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114309" :question/problem "$\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+4)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+4)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c09516b-ffde-5c4c-8dbe-564104924571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{15}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248513} {:answer/id #uuid "a581301a-72c3-5cfb-8ef1-56abefe481a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{25}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248900} {:answer/id #uuid "a5873c57-b416-5bd2-86d9-681f98615c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248901} {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae0e29-77f1-5100-a586-609d2c797e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{15}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea192b1-985a-504b-a59a-fe45ed09d88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d0e94f6-1e93-555f-a728-ca5181d50236" :question/math-academy-id "q-114312" :question/problem "$\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} {:answer/id #uuid "6f81ffd7-1892-5f9b-9320-925504438589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248407} {:answer/id #uuid "89d313a8-f000-577f-a816-a34a6622496f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248650} {:answer/id #uuid "a7092c76-1bc1-50c0-b6c7-d05f207eda48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248909} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f08285-93fd-5b63-ade9-e4f908688cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1b567b-6514-5d16-ba8c-83023f80f2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "062977fc-037b-5a67-9a07-c0d038a63f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114318" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[1-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771a4680-23b4-5532-bdca-e5e5e51c2e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248472} {:answer/id #uuid "788019d8-4726-57ee-8d3c-f8c472f663ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248481} {:answer/id #uuid "938dda6d-62d5-5932-8236-a8efaf7f79ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248736} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} {:answer/id #uuid "ac64494d-e051-58cd-912e-6906743c182e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc9c08d-e5e1-5b3f-9652-c2d450c9f225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ecbdeecb-1f0c-572b-8510-8e18414c1281" :question/math-academy-id "q-114320" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-2x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-2x}{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0{e}^{-2(0)}-(-1){e}^{-2(-1)}]-\\frac{3}{4}[{e}^{-2(0)}-{e}^{-2(-1)}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0+{e}^{2}]-\\frac{3}{4}[1-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d83e583-d218-50f4-abb7-474c6d01c304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247546} {:answer/id #uuid "3d047995-440b-51a6-837d-6a9c0a9dea33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247961} {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7776ae-27e1-5fb2-91d8-1d3d11b460fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248680} {:answer/id #uuid "aea67226-a698-5829-a7e0-c9089694e776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff430e6-479c-5fff-ae3c-19a79a5cfe3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37affd24-3b4f-536c-8927-723157249685" :question/math-academy-id "q-114328" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d8920c-9eae-5d0e-8971-ca7e7b55533e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-3}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248477} {:answer/id #uuid "7b577e2d-1a9b-598e-a5bb-8e6d22918919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248506} {:answer/id #uuid "82f9258b-b72f-566d-a506-e8c7094ed4bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248582} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} {:answer/id #uuid "fb407c98-f1d8-5183-b7e1-e23543be95c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf81a2af-d8b3-5358-9ec2-8ae5505c5bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e406eb1a-a97b-5da3-8a7a-44bb2a8c8ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-114329" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}9x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=9x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=9 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 9x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-3x}+3\\int {e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}9x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3x{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3}+3{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3}-{e}^{-3x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-3[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3(1/3)}-0\\cdot {e}^{-3\\cdot 0}]-[{e}^{-3(1/3)}-{e}^{-3\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =-3[\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{3}-0]-[{e}^{-1}-1] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{e}-\\frac{1}{e}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e-2}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47329e42-9fda-5dad-b1b7-b5de92199ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248057} {:answer/id #uuid "584e2ce7-69ed-515b-b3d8-ae953f17271d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248225} {:answer/id #uuid "90842d88-2e12-51f4-925b-763cbdc1a0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248708} {:answer/id #uuid "ad07dcb5-9bc9-5064-b6c1-d6071522fe76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248972} {:answer/id #uuid "df5f96e4-8268-56cf-9d0e-ec8e56b4e1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47329e42-9fda-5dad-b1b7-b5de92199ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248057} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7aa87d-cda1-557e-8fb5-e5baaeecced7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "447c75d4-22ec-5570-87c0-7a6b7bbeb6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114341" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(1,-5)$ and the line $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's draw a diagram describing our situation.  \n\n![](images/3a/3a4bbfd80480fe3fcc778a490514d27d65d83abf77ca1752e4203d9b3185b618.png)\n\nFirst, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3$ and passes through the point $(1,-5).$\n\nThe given line has a slope of $-\\frac{3}{2},$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+5 & =\\frac{2}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{2}{3}-5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 \\\\ y &=\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 & =\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{17}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{2}{3}x & =-\\frac{17}{3}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{13}{6}x & =-\\frac{26}{3} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{26}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{6}{13}) \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-3.$ So, our solution is $x=4$ and $y=-3.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(4,-3).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(1,-5)$ and $(4,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-1)^{2}+(-3+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(1,-5)$ and the line $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029577c8-4387-5dce-abc1-e362769c0f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247442} {:answer/id #uuid "4e18de69-f618-587b-a2ec-5220370f7b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248124} {:answer/id #uuid "8d733b4b-1dca-53a4-a8f8-a44dd6bcbc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248683} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c6caa-d5e0-51d2-ab76-a5150a905444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf847c0-a882-5640-8efa-f13f377ac775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a03c6caa-d5e0-51d2-ab76-a5150a905444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} :answer-field/id #uuid "e155ce82-9147-55f3-82af-e32fec80f54d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "590fb4d1-46ef-5eb8-ba9c-0c9e6a8189ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-114429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a05c2fc-f94d-5489-955e-6e93003cb216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247662} {:answer/id #uuid "a3dc3121-d85d-555d-95fa-e1f130a553c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248887} {:answer/id #uuid "a75bb911-b1a2-59de-ac5b-2d5b63e7d0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} {:answer/id #uuid "c53da061-88b8-5d38-9620-69fbe5f388d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249176} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bfdf52-8608-5e41-81ac-9c0e93199b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a75bb911-b1a2-59de-ac5b-2d5b63e7d0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} :answer-field/id #uuid "a980c72c-15a0-5296-ad73-7e85baf7f354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3841fdbd-8341-5e24-9f59-0d6b99ab3106" :question/math-academy-id "q-114441" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c892137-db18-57ab-a0c4-ee121e607cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2a7067-db8e-5098-bfe6-d1f90479e95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248104} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0a2abd-f164-5bc3-8dd3-b337d3b3b315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248389} {:answer/id #uuid "ad009786-2f7e-5893-ae43-3dd8c76182ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248969} {:answer/id #uuid "f843f5bd-ea3e-5dce-a8a3-d0d60b0e0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c892137-db18-57ab-a0c4-ee121e607cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0563b6-4107-5961-bf6f-8fdb92fa27b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ae308dc-8f77-58de-a2c1-ae20d02ecf13" :question/math-academy-id "q-114454" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2{csc}^{2}⁡x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{x}^{3}){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-[-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}] \\\\  & =-0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+2(1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3558fbac-1b59-57fe-9bd0-f677f28f907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247904} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbae598-1c6b-5eca-9ed6-66dceae7fb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c8c5c-01b7-553f-b6a2-1e3b22313e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248700} {:answer/id #uuid "d23ea027-eba2-500a-9470-4d37e94b1732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249290} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f3cf69-d025-571c-b710-5dfbc6ea9479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbae598-1c6b-5eca-9ed6-66dceae7fb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fe6922-c9ab-5e3a-bc26-b2f81f8df27d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dcffc55-70b6-5a56-9948-97e923b1fff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114460" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51767ce2-04dc-5c92-be64-ecdd456e4d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248156} {:answer/id #uuid "5af05724-0a68-584c-bdcc-e0f997546e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248248} {:answer/id #uuid "a32c58bd-145a-53ec-98dc-145783470c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248884} {:answer/id #uuid "b0502d42-a25a-5ae1-9cca-dcf3a4cbe860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} {:answer/id #uuid "c64da03c-c464-59cb-81c9-d62f5d957afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0502d42-a25a-5ae1-9cca-dcf3a4cbe860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22fa253-1174-584a-9758-f3f964e75c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91292256-4f82-5669-95d9-e91e8b8d6af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114552" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(x)({x}^{2})-\\int ({x}^{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aec5f05-d22a-5c56-9672-60bc96c1bb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247519} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5abc59-c7e4-5c8a-87f4-b54b803742a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247702} {:answer/id #uuid "35fbcfa4-611f-5481-a5a0-e26daf32fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247912} {:answer/id #uuid "3e70e2aa-5270-59bd-8d76-329cce6e0fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} {:answer/id #uuid "e913e7e7-7377-58f1-a576-f2631769debf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e70e2aa-5270-59bd-8d76-329cce6e0fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} :answer-field/id #uuid "258426ca-e1eb-5f21-b193-8a88f0107073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce30fbb-1b42-559b-a553-f2eb05e4f3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114553" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7ca2da-40f3-525c-bac6-b29d8480b2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247986} {:answer/id #uuid "a01808c9-616c-59db-89e8-974a2c400333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} {:answer/id #uuid "a30f743d-6b32-58c9-9c9b-527c9b8b888a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248883} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eb64cc-1ef2-5428-8c6b-e34b4c97b8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249336} {:answer/id #uuid "f65d4aa5-8ff1-5c46-aa50-cef0172e5477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a01808c9-616c-59db-89e8-974a2c400333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} :answer-field/id #uuid "80448976-ae2f-5f8d-b8a1-8ddcc578dda8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67ee7e99-c327-5643-bad9-04c09862c4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114556" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3338599f-b719-52ec-a42e-1f9c762d4c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247888} {:answer/id #uuid "9288729a-479e-5f0e-bb35-c0412ffb64f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248722} {:answer/id #uuid "b81fbb46-c0b8-52df-89da-8305c352443c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249071} {:answer/id #uuid "bb709158-d5c8-5b00-909d-3944db2f645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249097} {:answer/id #uuid "ff12fe3e-1160-52e7-95f0-ea194932f43e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb709158-d5c8-5b00-909d-3944db2f645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249097} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a5e92e-4b0f-5381-bbbe-52226a63a592" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "362beb84-a4c5-596a-b73b-e0ca0f79f0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-114557" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})-\\int (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c442b7-5812-5b9f-b5a3-9735de7bc5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} {:answer/id #uuid "a66e4f08-82a7-51c7-9f0f-a316a7a82095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248906} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1079b7-6c59-5146-a689-43939b214e55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248935} {:answer/id #uuid "c95f1123-d58f-569d-9f99-fc047c8ff23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249216} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5f9c6f-c38f-5d5f-aa01-a433d15de579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32c442b7-5812-5b9f-b5a3-9735de7bc5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} :answer-field/id #uuid "260a912a-e53c-57b3-a2f5-20d936d8b8f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "805d5bf3-56e5-56a7-8a77-c98eb5fe1df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114585" :question/problem "$\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int (\\frac{2x}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22097ee6-e029-5705-bd0d-12e8438e427a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247726} {:answer/id #uuid "3476300f-6f10-58d8-810a-76e72b26a106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247896} {:answer/id #uuid "46189a0d-05b3-5b4d-b076-027b366be2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248051} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a2c8c-0d41-5bdb-b6b2-87f65ad145c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248498} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5f4ac2-3246-5235-8484-0b0f64f2b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe5f4ac2-3246-5235-8484-0b0f64f2b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7889684-8ec7-5297-81fb-c1d9b326d8d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5747f9d-1d5b-5a68-8df4-e21d4a5aef56" :question/math-academy-id "q-114597" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06210c65-cc7a-5e4b-bf69-5482048cc94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247478} {:answer/id #uuid "1f8b6629-4046-5093-b11c-2c9ff8c296aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247704} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4a0cff-9e96-5852-b237-667134b904ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248828} {:answer/id #uuid "ade0ab9f-b410-5ccc-93ed-690c6b0b905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248978} {:answer/id #uuid "e484aeb9-9230-52f5-85a4-d8f264a2ce27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06210c65-cc7a-5e4b-bf69-5482048cc94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247478} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcabde0a-e8f2-56da-b3be-7871c9bb28e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16bb2470-b172-54fa-bb93-68ffa12f7218" :question/math-academy-id "q-114677" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bd605d-4c29-506c-8ce7-c84c48b67fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247627} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd43f9-d4db-533f-acd2-5f7163057588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247897} {:answer/id #uuid "481e05e7-b62d-5851-a787-6a5d10613a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} {:answer/id #uuid "8e50b12e-9d6e-5a6e-8673-a420a275d68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248690} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b9509-017e-5608-ad72-0fc4c95ad848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "481e05e7-b62d-5851-a787-6a5d10613a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a0c2c0-21f1-56dd-ac06-3f6bd57cc988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91699790-f225-57ae-8ea8-89f90b88a5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-114679" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv{|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x){|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot 1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-x{|}_{1/2}^{1}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0-(1-\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415bbc44-7f4c-58ad-8157-8f1f5ed47aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248005} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa4b914-459a-50f8-b61f-f8f5e3451572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248290} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc36f50-7f15-5f26-a2a4-236f583e6504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248521} {:answer/id #uuid "9025b8d7-d7e0-5ff3-b795-bc80c1e96b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248704} {:answer/id #uuid "b3394b3f-3533-568a-a273-e5b8ffd20f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415bbc44-7f4c-58ad-8157-8f1f5ed47aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248005} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fbb077-6af9-5c0d-a4c5-a794f5a7f75d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ba36d0b-ab92-5237-aa17-794cfb598845" :question/math-academy-id "q-114681" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "056d0b62-18e9-55f0-8775-8042d2ae824c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{2}+4x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247469} {:answer/id #uuid "4a24ad98-a0b5-5cc3-a600-8812772a324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-2x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248085} {:answer/id #uuid "75795d17-a5ee-582f-9b9e-c0ff0d8637fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248456} {:answer/id #uuid "ab67a9b5-9a63-5859-b7bb-9c8da59f41ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248948} {:answer/id #uuid "beb86753-1823-5658-bf1a-e594d3c2bfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}({x}^{2}-2x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab67a9b5-9a63-5859-b7bb-9c8da59f41ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248948} :answer-field/id #uuid "8047459c-94d3-55f6-8eca-48002be93179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1074dd87-580f-51cd-9b83-51cf6a648213" :question/math-academy-id "q-114693" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+1)(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2})(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-4\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(2x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-4(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(2x-1)+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{(4{x}^{2}+1){e}^{2x}}{2}-{e}^{2x}(2x-1)-4D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{2}-4x+3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-4D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189f9213-0590-5763-b7f1-5a9ff40545ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247646} {:answer/id #uuid "303bff0b-8c8d-570e-932f-08f4f7631376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247859} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec7d7a9-63ea-5dcf-a82f-7b1c3d305145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248132} {:answer/id #uuid "5779c8af-d348-5133-a80a-b74659af00bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} {:answer/id #uuid "df03a416-02ac-502d-9685-963bd71eb91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5779c8af-d348-5133-a80a-b74659af00bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} :answer-field/id #uuid "a867ef71-90c3-5a94-8b9a-8d5a238e8997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4cfdf230-d427-5945-b883-cca5a7c6a112" :question/math-academy-id "q-114698" :question/problem "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc23f83-d209-56fe-ba9f-4d4ea28149d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247528} {:answer/id #uuid "347405c1-4237-56c7-8c18-11e44217feec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247895} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7e723e-dbfd-5048-8cdb-9b45ca1d33f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247987} {:answer/id #uuid "d0824483-e541-59f6-a789-31210d1c98a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}(4{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249273} {:answer/id #uuid "e68c2af6-fc8e-55c4-a7ed-0bca24c425da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(2{x}^{2}+x+4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "347405c1-4237-56c7-8c18-11e44217feec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247895} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b20a23-0102-5d8b-a89a-d0ed94ee9a91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c03c84f2-a54b-5cd7-81f9-a3bec98efab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114699" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=1-2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56b4881f-232b-5196-af35-aea7cb58e62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248212} {:answer/id #uuid "5968f717-2e1f-500b-b4d7-ccdd473f65be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248233} {:answer/id #uuid "60480242-e3f6-5bd4-97c9-e03d8a634da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} {:answer/id #uuid "75629651-ad7e-5b79-a799-0589d593b3ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248455} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa029d1-b400-582d-911d-327f96487132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60480242-e3f6-5bd4-97c9-e03d8a634da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0fcafe-3643-59b7-8506-b7d096e4d110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638cdd8d-a193-51d5-8d07-1c091b8aea29" :question/math-academy-id "q-114709" :question/problem "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8e6af2-4d5c-5c2a-a223-b1581d70cf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247539} {:answer/id #uuid "81d0e0bb-c0c1-5d45-a394-2bbf8970a683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248575} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8ed56a-5c7f-5ef2-81bb-dd4b2068da0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248685} {:answer/id #uuid "b663df30-c9cb-50e7-be06-34aabcf17e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249056} {:answer/id #uuid "ec862b5c-e91d-5ccc-9ab8-a560591305a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec862b5c-e91d-5ccc-9ab8-a560591305a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd4bc8-95db-5454-a58a-0b3490f1540b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f620a8f2-ded3-5ab5-a180-a9e0b77ecbff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114712" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f54fcd2-11eb-5de2-b3f7-146de7b6348a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+2{log}_{4}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247564} {:answer/id #uuid "407f3c19-f6db-5e87-b664-92774974ae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247993} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0cac64-7a75-5a03-b08a-cee4bcbfa551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248695} {:answer/id #uuid "d24d95fe-f787-520e-9b19-d413da18936f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249291} {:answer/id #uuid "e86cde0d-e490-5e48-8a63-d7e0865c34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e86cde0d-e490-5e48-8a63-d7e0865c34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477} :answer-field/id #uuid "e420d51c-8836-5780-9cc3-1975930de065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40de2008-379c-588d-bf38-59107f150b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-114880" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{4}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0566e525-d41b-5762-abad-a35a60fcea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247468} {:answer/id #uuid "377a31ef-b562-5a6f-805e-2834d145cfda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247923} {:answer/id #uuid "928f1290-d85e-54cd-bd20-3cfebd037b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248724} {:answer/id #uuid "db06656d-5fcf-5439-bdb0-133473765928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff3e4b-d499-52d7-802f-f1d97113fff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff3e4b-d499-52d7-802f-f1d97113fff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddcf16bb-2de3-57be-904f-fe6f88d0b63a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25b1fd19-3728-5b2c-98ff-e3d6d85297ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114883" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D) \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[e{ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{3})-6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})+18e]-[(1){ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{3})-6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})+18(1)] \\\\  & =9e-18e+18e-18 \\\\  & =9e-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bbba15-3ca2-548d-aa0b-fa8fde96be41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247648} {:answer/id #uuid "505545e5-5b59-5235-b0a9-6bfde088dc5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248143} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1c7d6f-7d36-5780-986c-93149710dad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248533} {:answer/id #uuid "7e81ded9-2f3b-592a-8788-962d13bc36f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248537} {:answer/id #uuid "abfdae4f-4dff-5106-9d49-8bae29e9c2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abfdae4f-4dff-5106-9d49-8bae29e9c2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248954} :answer-field/id #uuid "a24575db-05cf-5008-adac-d417701d5102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "759dad06-62ad-59d4-9d65-70a46d8005a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114892" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 & -4 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & 3 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} & =3-\\frac{(\\frac{17}{2})}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{17}{2x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[3x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3(2-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(2)+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(0)+3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})] \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d2a00f-4a5e-50ec-95a7-3d34717ca878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}[3-11\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247508} {:answer/id #uuid "4193cca1-11ab-5816-befe-e6e7082fd2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}[1-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248007} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff3945d-cc27-5c31-8969-8fc40195197f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}[4-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248409} {:answer/id #uuid "94b6c9b3-1db7-55a8-8ada-45bd1cf3adf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248746} {:answer/id #uuid "ca649297-0c30-5fd0-a460-252be27d14b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}[17-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b6c9b3-1db7-55a8-8ada-45bd1cf3adf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248746} :answer-field/id #uuid "e407e99d-a50c-5c35-b3e1-dbdcca77665b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf68c363-607b-5ed8-bb76-a69145831fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-114894" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 2 & 5 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{17}{3})}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(2+\\frac{17}{3x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\text{d}x+17{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[2x+\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(0-(-1))+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(-1)-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(1)+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{34}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9826cc-221a-58f0-a949-003259d10830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247516} {:answer/id #uuid "1935d4e4-d30d-5335-ab50-3b3fa04366e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247651} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9aeadf-fded-5a2b-861d-58af4c73c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247959} {:answer/id #uuid "54ac800d-c455-530d-b963-3aea2be7c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248185} {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226bde-c895-54e8-98cf-b5b2df79f6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "462b058c-0216-5b9a-aa39-6bb6d7bc768e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b73f700-d96a-599b-ab52-2db5d3386e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247811} {:answer/id #uuid "3bfc4874-a112-5f03-a9d1-39829d4222c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[2-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247956} {:answer/id #uuid "4924bf57-6609-582a-b504-14c54c2c2e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248075} {:answer/id #uuid "55342b69-6990-55a7-b6b9-79464a3e57e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248192} {:answer/id #uuid "9991218e-5d69-54aa-88aa-8ca966e8ab5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4924bf57-6609-582a-b504-14c54c2c2e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248075} :answer-field/id #uuid "4388d5da-7f71-581a-8f21-f145c319a5de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e67ca108-b4a2-50be-81c1-fe32c84586b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114898" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 8 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} & =8+\\frac{3}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =8+\\frac{12}{4x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}(8+\\frac{12}{4x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\text{d}x+12{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-1|]_{-1/8}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(0-(-\\frac{1}{8}))+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(-\\frac{1}{8})-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(\\frac{1}{8})+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082f5ffa-db8f-5b86-9f1f-66bec8888277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247495} {:answer/id #uuid "312a7284-86a2-58d1-925a-aae469b9cc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247869} {:answer/id #uuid "4646f294-569b-5c9a-8e3f-8b4bffc32dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248052} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ab61f-f876-54ff-ac9a-719572398e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} {:answer/id #uuid "aed8ce21-2fef-51ea-932a-bf3d76234eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ab61f-f876-54ff-ac9a-719572398e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} :answer-field/id #uuid "90297971-15bc-5633-a065-ce4100255f03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dca36867-5a6f-51bd-9e64-ad043dde12a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114900" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(2{x}^{2})-\\int (2{x}^{2})(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$ \n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2-2+1)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0188c738-8d3f-5f42-b61d-b6905e5bfdd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247429} {:answer/id #uuid "3788c026-240f-51ce-96e4-36b327b09c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247924} {:answer/id #uuid "52b4f6b7-1404-5c2e-b939-52278a731f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{9})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248167} {:answer/id #uuid "7654b839-b02e-5d72-8ce8-e1293aaa3cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248466} {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf4ce-721d-5f9e-8dc0-70a1acafef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf4ce-721d-5f9e-8dc0-70a1acafef73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249050} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8f6cff-c895-5917-993d-b2d120420f39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c6784ae-fdbb-5b66-87d7-0cf88bfc85a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114910" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+18 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+18 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+18 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-3}{3}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-3}{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63035e67-c066-56f1-897a-8d319b27f7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248321} {:answer/id #uuid "728659a8-4d30-5f53-b783-77ca68417d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248426} {:answer/id #uuid "7c54a2d2-9684-516e-a49e-05b02d5d4c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248517} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa8f858-6398-51a7-9ffc-de9e24072ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248942} {:answer/id #uuid "c56cf019-abf9-5371-bc50-d8f4dfad801e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c54a2d2-9684-516e-a49e-05b02d5d4c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248517} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa53ad0f-77f4-501c-a778-132511875487" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efd4eb6a-b650-553c-bcc2-ab2b63a8dbe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114918" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{(6x+1)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4(1-(6x+1)^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{6x+1}{2}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{6x+1}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31c17a05-d2f9-5ba0-b754-dcbfc7f9b4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-3}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247879} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccaaf30-f65e-532d-85cd-8c1ce995b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248111} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1dda95-180f-5a89-bfe9-5307962c3d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} {:answer/id #uuid "c56c203a-3635-5203-8a26-4d2596b69db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249180} {:answer/id #uuid "ec86287a-069c-51b9-9eb7-959c7a23a3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(2(x-3))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1dda95-180f-5a89-bfe9-5307962c3d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} :answer-field/id #uuid "83644fa9-f278-5c29-b9fd-b62b8c892acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d48157cd-3ea4-5a4b-b2a2-ea19ff6fa51b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114923" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001d516e-ba06-5b95-b4a6-f35dab9a3672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247415} {:answer/id #uuid "14ed51ee-756e-57ce-98c5-e09580d0ea4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247613} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6dbd24-53a8-57ca-8ab3-2c785beb7617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd72e51-75ac-59c4-906c-a14dfbeed5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247990} {:answer/id #uuid "4deeee7d-3bfe-54f3-bb50-f18cec4519b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+4}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d6dbd24-53a8-57ca-8ab3-2c785beb7617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} :answer-field/id #uuid "8347f822-40d4-57c9-9262-ff4fdf512681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07920739-bd19-5b4b-b343-8e19ac7c6d5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114928" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-8x+16)-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-4.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069e5dc3-903f-56c3-80b2-a36d93cb6a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247483} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee8a822-9e03-5b0b-9157-4a6e261fd6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(2(x+2))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248134} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9b7170-e2cb-5afb-ae16-7aa25d17f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} {:answer/id #uuid "8c688811-e631-576f-b3af-fccf1d19453f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248679} {:answer/id #uuid "c73082f2-4cbb-5c23-891d-47290806832d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-2}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9b7170-e2cb-5afb-ae16-7aa25d17f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} :answer-field/id #uuid "76fa23d1-4298-5709-9837-39a75683bfac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd2cd352-82c1-595a-88b3-99447daccebc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114929" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c50259-96ff-5091-b6d8-d010aabcd87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2}-3}{4{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247435} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1b58be-7936-591f-a3c9-e22825f21d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248249} {:answer/id #uuid "602d95a8-3c49-5628-a5fc-26ae6d4442af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248293} {:answer/id #uuid "ae45cdbd-b5db-5833-8170-fccfe8733b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} {:answer/id #uuid "f16fc0ad-7654-55ab-873b-8984cf712d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae45cdbd-b5db-5833-8170-fccfe8733b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} :answer-field/id #uuid "46bceeef-1e66-56f1-87c4-0b40ebcc4c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7237523-38ec-5167-93d0-30747905ffb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114942" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}(3{x}^{3})-\\int (3{x}^{3})(\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{6D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3-2+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(0-0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f84bc89-0f5f-5174-b311-6b1ac207d432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} {:answer/id #uuid "acd12eca-de9b-50f1-ae82-10635e26c184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-6}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248968} {:answer/id #uuid "f04115a5-6b2e-5bc2-9ed5-4e7dbb828a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249532} {:answer/id #uuid "f2594c73-abaa-58dd-995b-af12abd8461c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249549} {:answer/id #uuid "f538ac92-7bb7-5776-a593-eda1db9ee897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e+3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f84bc89-0f5f-5174-b311-6b1ac207d432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1851a2-09ca-5e98-9283-451c4f3c0948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee94ab2f-1f66-5795-8930-e1ab98c8dab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114944" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\int (x)(\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(4-8+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101c128a-6dc8-5632-a7ae-f0b91b164739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{5}+3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247565} {:answer/id #uuid "2adceece-a53a-577c-9b55-b2e47ed35eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247806} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5aca5e-dc8e-5ba7-9af6-c2a386609510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247817} {:answer/id #uuid "a227ec20-ef2b-5e2e-b4e4-2aca175b50f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248872} {:answer/id #uuid "dbbef6d4-187f-5f47-a784-698d678b5e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{5}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a227ec20-ef2b-5e2e-b4e4-2aca175b50f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248872} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3c2387-20aa-5008-8cd7-6fc006779faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d87d568c-f1e1-5dbc-b0f7-7053ed2197d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114946" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=25{x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(5{x}^{5})-\\int (5{x}^{5})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10(\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D) \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-10D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{5})]-[{1}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{5})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5-2+\\frac{2}{5})]-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21fa41e6-4e3a-5806-859d-c2aaa4b58edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247725} {:answer/id #uuid "3aad9910-8581-517c-bee6-27e599bcdafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247943} {:answer/id #uuid "81ff4d92-1a10-5646-988f-1c901a51022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e5a27-6ad8-5b1a-b327-7847f10b1222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248844} {:answer/id #uuid "cefcf51a-b70a-5c3a-a3be-b1a5d98e9adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ff4d92-1a10-5646-988f-1c901a51022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} :answer-field/id #uuid "6117be46-83ef-580f-84ce-56c76fa2d084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f09819e-da12-5415-9b7c-4388f9ed375d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114952" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522547ac-6535-5fb0-b8a3-a2053a87b01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248161} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffb7ca-1a66-52ae-b04f-97ae522f8f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248279} {:answer/id #uuid "751980ea-1704-5381-ae28-6aa05cfad2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} {:answer/id #uuid "90fe0781-abfd-56c8-9147-cf8bdbde8121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248713} {:answer/id #uuid "9d475fa0-a4da-59e4-b41c-47c13378b87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "751980ea-1704-5381-ae28-6aa05cfad2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0704fd5-1897-52d9-acd5-2f3d7565c6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85a3e0f2-59ad-5501-8562-0840b6094216" :question/math-academy-id "q-114965" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{6}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{6}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I \\\\ 7I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡(e)-{ln}^{7}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0432af-5e36-5fda-8917-32b349683fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247816} {:answer/id #uuid "38592cbc-383b-5e42-b2c1-16c799f4dac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247927} {:answer/id #uuid "472b2169-b73e-52b2-a759-79ee2c0017dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248056} {:answer/id #uuid "a124094c-2198-56e3-a44a-8e218a714881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248864} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c76c8f-f2d8-5896-8bd2-98aa7de77cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c76c8f-f2d8-5896-8bd2-98aa7de77cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfceba82-e7c8-58e8-a6e1-6dbed0dd06ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aafbcc52-b05c-5248-b40a-c0ce083a128b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114999" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{9}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{9}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I \\\\ 10I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡(e)-{ln}^{10}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018d8348-3190-5eea-b417-c63541e4aff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247430} {:answer/id #uuid "08eab5fa-3385-5df5-b8fd-2f29432c498e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247499} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb0449b-6ed5-5ab7-9e17-f2f9074c0612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247696} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1524c0-3b53-58d5-b338-ecb0ead5ac3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247832} {:answer/id #uuid "67f62f68-93fb-55cb-a9ad-f01fff119dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "018d8348-3190-5eea-b417-c63541e4aff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247430} :answer-field/id #uuid "078894b3-54fc-5c41-9c56-f018aef4c9b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9725f40a-ccc5-5b84-9193-a09e8482b8d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115218" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1}\\le \\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1} & \\le \\frac{1}{9} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1} & \\le \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x+1}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ (x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ (x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ (x+1)(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\le -\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & \\ge \\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302b378f-be12-5ba0-97fd-06dd7fe61909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247858} {:answer/id #uuid "3173ff57-51bd-5dc4-8c31-633792b6a1b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247872} {:answer/id #uuid "433231b9-72f8-5a2a-b270-d72099dbaf75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248027} {:answer/id #uuid "cb82884c-5f42-579d-a3b2-766dcd5e9b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249235} {:answer/id #uuid "f6af4d9b-c12c-51d1-a663-b88288cd8554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302b378f-be12-5ba0-97fd-06dd7fe61909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247858} :answer-field/id #uuid "759dac82-e131-5166-b8ec-519724d4e077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac4b46ad-428b-596b-a6dd-aa26aa057694" :question/math-academy-id "q-115222" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1\\ge 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}+1 & \\ge 2 \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6} & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x+6}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ (x+6)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+6)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6) & \\le \\frac{0}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ x+6 & \\le 0 \\\\ x & \\le -6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bddbba4-895d-5993-b7ec-55a01d328fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247530} {:answer/id #uuid "50e8f068-fe0e-581f-8ae4-9a985a1bdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248151} {:answer/id #uuid "52bdc298-cd04-5aaf-a6fa-fcf496dbdd22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248169} {:answer/id #uuid "6c791cdd-bf14-5cdc-a55a-2374ab3e0790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248383} {:answer/id #uuid "78b2b35b-752c-54d4-a1db-65d499c76704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e8f068-fe0e-581f-8ae4-9a985a1bdef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248151} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdff120-3f6b-5674-abcd-9423a762d861" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef8ebb72-c9f4-522b-b5c8-2cd601e5dcba" :question/math-academy-id "q-115233" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1<-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}+1 & <-5 \\\\ 2{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-6 \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7} & <-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $\\frac{1}{3}>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nTherefore, ${(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}$ cannot be less than $-3.$ Hence, the inequality\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2x+7}<-3\n$$\n\nhas no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e749b95-3859-5caf-bfd8-c834793e8ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247694} {:answer/id #uuid "40bebdef-ae8a-5d9e-ac28-6228e738db2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247995} {:answer/id #uuid "49f23bbb-2f76-5966-bbae-3c9d22acc9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248082} {:answer/id #uuid "b99ff983-b6ef-5e58-8aa0-af927de0b3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249083} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b0c71b-a6be-59ae-b32b-dde21ce862fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f23bbb-2f76-5966-bbae-3c9d22acc9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248082} :answer-field/id #uuid "7730106b-6087-572a-9b32-b26564608b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c08f0a1-4fee-59ab-b31f-f6a9816dc7a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115250" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${5}^{x-1}<{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x-1} & <{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-1}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2-x}] \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(2-x)(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\ (x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & <x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x & <\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e785456-0d46-526f-9e67-18d57eadc06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247557} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9b3b46-47ed-564d-81ee-53957c02a43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247803} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbce6e1-d015-5841-ac53-b3bc03022688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248277} {:answer/id #uuid "cecf1feb-5477-5f51-924d-678fd3092009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249257} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bba209-bdae-5fcc-b9cd-f07175cf1210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbce6e1-d015-5841-ac53-b3bc03022688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5dba1e-963f-540d-840f-945c1bcdcb43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "804e099a-7eac-522b-b475-41496ab8d992" :question/math-academy-id "q-115323" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x-10=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)-10 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)-10 & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ -10 & =-2A-2 \\\\ -2A & =-8 \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-2(-\\frac{1}{x-2})+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a329a54-4f81-5bc7-9972-9d32effaa6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248241} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7e6dcd-4341-5ca3-9e25-273a9f542d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248963} {:answer/id #uuid "b68ce2f4-36aa-5333-97d7-e92257913ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249059} {:answer/id #uuid "d9433e5e-716b-5504-ac6b-94eed855c88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249342} {:answer/id #uuid "e443c042-27a8-5be0-ac68-ea847b0c1a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9433e5e-716b-5504-ac6b-94eed855c88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249342} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e01a2f-c7f0-58e1-95b2-bb107a5aa3e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dfebbb3-1e7f-58e9-a0ac-939acd360f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-115415" :question/problem "![](images/52/52b283fd5a8d9f374fad0a007f127598b86c53d7acf4df05d1415589e43faaa0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(3,1).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,1),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=1$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(1) \\\\ 9 & =4p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ffa276-379e-5b1f-ade7-d6d1a255f79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247460} {:answer/id #uuid "213191af-0b1c-54df-85c1-bfc33aa407a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247717} {:answer/id #uuid "367a9704-d0cd-52a6-8c9e-1f43b931615b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247915} {:answer/id #uuid "75227f58-c686-5197-87a0-5b1edfb5b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{2}{25}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248454} {:answer/id #uuid "c5048ebb-d0b2-50a9-9408-f2aac2c86149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367a9704-d0cd-52a6-8c9e-1f43b931615b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247915} :answer-field/id #uuid "8461e255-e863-501e-bc4f-d4c3f00fa748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "913fe829-246c-5859-8570-cf82a68a6df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115420" :question/problem "![](images/41/410da7fdbf283aba57c2000a37c56a87e11ed1b1372183a1d3c808376dba495f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,2).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 25 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{25}{8})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094e6092-339d-5805-b65a-0ba9ea32fcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247504} {:answer/id #uuid "14563ff8-ab85-58f1-81f8-f36ec51e3961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247607} {:answer/id #uuid "469c754e-d524-520c-ab78-58d1d9ef15b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248054} {:an